  "measurement_definitions": {
    "reviewed_article": "Distinct article with its latest terminal outcome in the window equal to published, rejected or held; each subject counted once even if retried.",
    "throughput_timestamp": "Workflow finished_at within the inclusive window bounds. Current-generation progress is separate from window throughput.",
    "model_call_timestamp": "AIModelCallLog.created_at within the inclusive window bounds. Logs record application attempts, not necessarily one HTTP request each.",
    "activity_timestamp": "AIWorkItem.finished_at within the inclusive window bounds. Activity completion and call-log counts can differ at boundaries and through retries.",
    "occupied_permits": "Unexpired, leased, non-health AIWorkItem rows across all dispatcher owners; not real-time HTTP sockets or measured HTTP concurrency.",
    "capacity_denominator": "Both denominators are retained: configured capacity remains 157 permits (47100 permit-seconds in the final 300 seconds); routable capacity excludes routes cooling down at each observation and is integrated over the same window. CTM-M3 was cooling down at three early final-window samples, giving an estimated routable denominator of 47057.083 permit-seconds. Existing leases can remain valid during a later route cooldown.",
    "time_weighting": "Piecewise linear interpolation of sampled counts; trapezoidal integration clipped to the exact stated window. The final-window start is interpolated using the bracketing snapshots. This is a sampling estimate, not exact continuous occupancy.",
    "peak": "Largest observed value among actual samples inside the stated window; unsampled peaks may be higher.",
    "held_backlog": "Exact eligibility-filtered, fingerprint-aware unchanged-hold check; raw hold metadata is not used as a substitute."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Batch size 8 baseline only. The later batch size 32 deployment and its measurements are excluded.",
    "The early one-minute diagnostic and final five-minute throughput are separate evidence windows; their rates must not be interchanged.",
    "Permits can cover scheduling, provider work and durable completion. Their occupation fraction is not HTTP throughput or provider utilization.",
    "Summary waiting/skipped outcomes do not count as successful AI reviews. A completed summary drain can be followed by a new drain, so it does not imply all source content is permanently resolved.",
    "The ETA estimates one review pass over currently eligible, non-parked articles, including items already in flight; newly held articles count as pass completion. It does not promise all review content will be published or rejected.",
    "Unchanged held content and missing abstracts have no automatic-clearance ETA. Evidence or enrichment must change first.",
    "ETA assumes the observed rate persists and no new eligible arrivals; short-window production rates are not a controlled causal comparison.",
    "No article text, request/response content, task identifiers, credentials, provider URLs or host connection details are exported."
  ]
